margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["8 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a scope/AC item requiring the recreated installer to resolve the scanner prefix to an absolute path (e.g. make _link_semgrep target absolute, or have the prefix boundary call .resolve()) plus a regression test that invokes the installer with a RELATIVE --prefix from a different cwd and asserts bin/semgrep is executable — so the advisory lane can actually reach and run the nine contracts.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.265,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Incident 90c7 comment #10 (read-only diagnosis): '_link_semgrep (install_review_scanners.py:328-339) does link.symlink_to(semgrep) ... a relative symlink target is resolved relative to the symlink's OWN DIRECTORY, so the link ... DANGLES' and 'pytest NEVER RAN. Execution died inside the install step's own post-install version verification (Makefile:503)'.","The Makefile passed a RELATIVE prefix: REVIEW_SCANNER_PREFIX := .tools/review-scanners, while DEFAULT_PREFIX is absolute — so only the Makefile call path is broken; local runs with no --prefix pass, which is why it escaped.","Ticket b973 reparent comment: 'the nine SCANNER_INTEGRATION_NODES contracts are UNTESTED, not failing — a materially different starting point for any re-land.'","The plan's Testing section and ACs mention manifest selection, checksum/hash rejection, and contract execution, but never the relative-prefix symlink resolution defect."],"finding":"The plan recreates the reverted scanner installer 'as a starting point' but does not require fixing the latent relative-prefix symlink defect that (per the incident's read-only diagnosis) prevented the nine scanner contracts from ever executing — so the recreated advisory lane would fail on main for the same reason and never produce the passing run ADR 0114 requires.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbecf935dff0be637","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope ('Recreate the reverted scanner artifacts from change 2612 as a starting point') + AC line 'Valid selected scanner locks allow the explicit native-binary target to run the real Semgrep/Gitleaks integration contracts'","norm_id":"n6a3cecd88156dbe2","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The advisory scanner lane runs on a full-route Gerrit patchset (or on main) and dies in the installer's post-install semgrep version check with 'could not execute .tools/review-scanners/bin/semgrep', so the nine contracts never execute and ADR 0114's required passing-on-main run is never obtained.","A future promotion change is blocked because there is no green advisory run to cite as the promotion precondition."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Resolve the prefix once at the boundary so every downstream path (bin dir, semgrep-venv, symlink target) is absolute regardless of how --prefix was spelled, and add the relative-prefix-from-other-cwd regression test that the original tests missed (they only exercised the absolute DEFAULT_PREFIX). State this as an explicit adaptation of the reverted installer rather than a verbatim recreation.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_